; DOMAIN: partition-complex [CLOSED, derived 2026-07-24]
; Claim: The partition complex |Pi_n| is the nerve of the poset of proper nontrivial partitions of {1..n}, a finite Sigma_n-space equivalent to a wedge of (n-1)! spheres S^{n-3} (Sigma_n-equivariantly, up to a sign/regular-representation twist). Its role: the n-th Goodwillie derivative of the identity functor of pointed spaces is del_n(Id) = D(Sigma^inf |Pi_n|^diamond)^{shift} — Spanier-Whitehead dual of the (suspended) partition complex, a spectrum with Sigma_n-action. Equivalently the layers D_n(Id)(X) = Omega^inf (del_n(Id) wedge X^{wedge n})_{hSigma_n} are governed by this equivariant sphere. The partition poset is a Tits-building analogue (Cohen-Macaulay, its reduced homology concentrated in top degree carries the Sigma_n-Lie representation Lie(n)); del_n(Id) is the Koszul/Spanier-Whitehead dual of the Lie operad, linking Goodwillie calculus to operads and the Lie representation.
; Bridge: genesis_goodwillie (partition complex IS the derivative del_n(Id) of the identity functor; closes the Taylor-tower-of-Id computation) + genesis_stable_homotopy (del_n(Id) is a spectrum with Sigma_n-action, Spanier-Whitehead duality in the stable category) + genesis_homology (the poset's reduced homology, concentrated in top degree = Lie(n) representation, is computed via the order/chain complex of the partition lattice).
(= (partition-complex $n) (nerve (proper-partitions $n)))
(= (equivariant-homotopy-type $n) (wedge-of-spheres (factorial (minus $n 1)) (minus $n 3)))
(= (identity-derivative $n) (spanier-whitehead-dual (suspension-spectrum (partition-complex $n))))
(= (top-homology-representation $n) (lie-representation $n))
(= (goodwillie-layer-of-id $n $X) (infinite-loop-space (homotopy-orbits (smash (identity-derivative $n) (smash-power $X $n)) (symmetric-group $n))))